INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS
=========================

PREREQUISITES
-------------
- OMNeT++ 6.0.2 or later (https://omnetpp.org/download/)
- C++17 compiler (GCC 9+ or Clang 10+)
- See REQUIREMENTS.md for full details


QUICK START (Command Line)
--------------------------
1. Clone the repository:
   # FiCo4OMNeT (with the CAN-FD extension) is included in this repository
   cd FiCo4OMNeT

2. Ensure OMNeT++ is in your PATH:
   source /path/to/omnetpp/setenv

3. Generate makefiles:
   make makefiles

4. Build:
   make                    # Debug build
   make MODE=release       # Release build

5. Run an example:
   cd examples/can/basic
   ./run


QUICK START (OMNeT++ IDE)
-------------------------
1. Open OMNeT++ IDE

2. Import project:
   File → Import → General → Existing Projects into Workspace
   Select the CANFD_Omnet directory
   Do NOT check "Copy projects into workspace"

3. Build:
   Press Ctrl+B (or Project → Build All)

4. Run simulation:
   Navigate to examples/can/basic/
   Right-click omnetpp.ini → Run As → OMNeT++ Simulation


RUNNING EXAMPLES
----------------
Several ready-to-run examples are provided:

  examples/can/basic/       - Basic CAN network
  examples/heterogeneous/   - Mixed CAN + CAN-FD traffic

Each example directory contains:
  - omnetpp.ini: Simulation configuration
  - *.ned: Network topology definition
  - run: Shell script to launch simulation


TROUBLESHOOTING
---------------
If make fails with "nedtool not found":
  → Ensure OMNeT++ setenv has been sourced

If simulation crashes at startup:
  → Rebuild with: make clean && make

For IDE indexer issues:
  → Right-click project → Index → Rebuild


NOTES
-----
- The build creates a shared library (libFiCo4OMNeT.so) in src/
- Adding/removing source files requires: make makefiles
- Generated files (*_m.cc, *_m.h) are auto-created from .msg files
